statement:
Let P, m ∈ ℕ, write ℝ^k = Euclid k with the Euclidean norm |·|, and let G : ℝ^m → ℝ^P be of class C¹ (ContDiff ℝ 1 G). Let x ∈ ℝ^m be a point at which the derivative DG(x) = fderiv ℝ G x : ℝ^m → ℝ^P is injective. Then there is r > 0 with two properties:
- G is injective on the closed ball B̄_r(x) = {z : |z − x| ≤ r};
- DG(z) is injective for every z ∈ B̄_r(x).
